  "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n24+x=9\n$$\n\nNow, let's rewrite the left-hand side so that it's similar to what we've seen before.\n\n$$\nx+24=9\n$$\n\nTo isolate $x$, we need to perform the *opposite* of adding $24$ to $x$, which is *subtracting* $24$ from $x.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+24 & =9 \\\\ x+24-24 & =9-24 \\\\ x+0 & =-15 \\\\ x & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
